# Spring Security + JWT — Project Notes

## 1. Objective

We added **Spring Security + JWT-based authentication and authorization** to the LangChain4j Spring Boot project.

The goal was to make the project more realistic by having:

* User authentication
* MongoDB-based users
* User roles
* JWT token generation
* JWT validation
* Stateless security
* Protected employee APIs
* Role-based authorization

High-level architecture:

```text
Client
  |
  | POST /auth/login
  | username + password
  v
Spring Security
  |
  v
AuthenticationManager
  |
  v
UserDetailsService
  |
  v
MongoDB
  |
  | User + password + role
  v
Authentication successful
  |
  v
JwtService
  |
  v
JWT Token
  |
  v
Client
```

For subsequent requests:

```text
Client
  |
  | Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
  v
JwtAuthenticationFilter
  |
  v
Extract JWT
  |
  v
Validate JWT
  |
  v
Load UserDetails
  |
  v
Create Authentication
  |
  v
SecurityContextHolder
  |
  v
Authorization
  |
  v
Controller
```

