# 8. Security Configuration

We configured Spring Security using a `SecurityFilterChain`.

Important concepts:

```java
.authorizeHttpRequests(...)
```

controls authorization.

For example:

```java
.requestMatchers("/auth/**").permitAll()
```

means login/authentication endpoints can be accessed without authentication.

And:

```java
.requestMatchers("/employees/**").authenticated()
```

means employee APIs require an authenticated user.

We also configured:

```java
.csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
```

for our stateless REST API design.

And:

```java
.sessionManagement(...)
```

with:

```text
SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS
```

