# 16. SecurityContextHolder

One of the most important Spring Security concepts learned during this debugging.

For the current request, Spring Security keeps authentication information in:

```java
SecurityContextHolder
```

Conceptually:

```text
JWT
 |
 v
JwtAuthenticationFilter
 |
 v
Authentication
 |
 v
SecurityContextHolder
 |
 v
Authorization
 |
 v
Controller
```

Before our JWT filter was correctly registered:

```text
SecurityContextHolder
        |
        v
Anonymous
```

After fixing the filter:

```text
SecurityContextHolder
        |
        v
Authenticated User
```

This explains why the endpoint changed from `403` to working correctly.

